              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tracy Carll"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent cake. Substituted applesauce and coconut oil in place of Mayo. Also made in a 10X15 pan and topped with cream cheese frosting. Delicious",
            "datePublished": "2021-02-22T01:43:35.010Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LMWC"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this yesterday for a late family Christmas get together. It was amazing. I made it as a 9x 13 sheet cake. Baked 350 degrees for about 35 min. That is when my toothpick came out clean. I used walnuts because I did not have pecans. I found a basic cream cheese icing. The icing called for 1 tsp of vanilla extract, I used 1/4 tsp of almond extract and 3/4 tsp of vanilla. Everyone went for seconds. Definitly a keeper!",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-08T15:48:43.379Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ksg"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this cake twice already. The first time followed the recipe exactly. It was great the first day when just baked. But when I ate the leftovers out of the fridge the next day, the cake totally changed consistency. It was hard and too dense. Warming it in the microwave for a few secs set it right. Guess the mayo sort of solidified in the fridge or something. The next time, instead of mayo used 1/2 cup vegetable oil and 1/2 cup applesauce. This time it was perfect. Great flavor and texture even the next day straight out of the fridge.",
            "datePublished": "2014-07-26T17:58:13.493Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BeeJayEf"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made it and it is the best carrot cake ever (sorry, Mom)! I added 2/3 cup of chopped pecans and used a 13\"x9\" cake pan instead of the 8\" round pans. I was in a hurry so I used a cheesecake frosting out of a can. Really easy to make. This recipe is a keeper and I know it would make awesome cupcakes.",
            "datePublished": "2019-06-17T23:26:42.320Z"
